okf_version: "1.0"
task: "Before implementing the codex-desktop runtime: prove, by running it, how the Codex desktop app (MSIX OpenAI.Codex 26.915.4065.0, app\\ChatGPT.exe) can be isolated, routed and fed turns from outside."
reported: "User, 2026-09-23: 'codex app desktop 버전도 실행 런타임으로 지원'; chose a separate CODEX_HOME and channel SSE injection."
confirmed:
  env_reaches_the_app: "ChatGPT.exe started directly from its WindowsApps path with UseShellExecute=false inherits the caller's environment: CODEX_HOME pointed at a scratch folder filled with state_5.sqlite, logs_2.sqlite, memories/goals/queue sqlite and the bundled plugin marketplace."
  second_instance_needs_user_data_dir: "With only CODEX_ELECTRON_USER_DATA_PATH set, the new process printed 'Opening in existing browser session.' and exited - Chromium's process singleton handed off to the user's running instance (pid 83404). Adding the switch --user-data-dir=<same path> gives a separate, fully working instance next to the user's; the user's instance stayed up throughout."
  ws_app_server: "With CODEX_APP_SERVER_WS_URL=ws://127.0.0.1:19731 the app spawns no codex.exe of its own and connects to an app-server we started (`codex.exe app-server --listen ws://127.0.0.1:19731`, CODEX_HOME = the isolated home); app log 'Starting app-server connection hostId=local transport=websocket' ... 'Codex CLI initialized'."
  startup_order: "If the app-server is not listening when the app starts, the app shows 'ChatGPT failed to start. connect ECONNREFUSED 127.0.0.1:19731' and keeps the main window hidden even after a later reconnect succeeds. The launcher must wait for http://127.0.0.1:<port>/readyz (200) first."
  child_lifetime: "An app-server started with redirected stdout/stderr pipes died when the starting PowerShell exited; started with file redirection it stayed up. The launcher must not tie the server to pipes nobody drains."
  auth: "Copying ~/.codex/auth.json into the isolated home was enough: account/read returned type chatgpt, planType pro, and the app UI came up signed in (no browser login)."
  second_client: "A second JSON-RPC client on the same ws URL works only without an Origin header - websocket-client's default Origin got 'Handshake status 403 Forbidden'; suppress_origin=True was accepted. initialize -> account/read -> thread/loaded/list -> thread/start{cwd} -> turn/start all answered."
  ui_follows_second_client: "The thread started by the second client appeared in the app's Recents immediately (cwd C:\\Users\\djlov\\ciel-runtime), and turn/start produced turn/started, item/completed(userMessage), turn/completed notifications. That turn failed upstream only because the scratch config said model = \"gpt-5\" ('not supported when using Codex with a ChatGPT account') - a probe-config artefact, not the injection path."
  rollout: "The isolated home's rollout recorded session_meta originator=\"Codex Desktop\", source=\"vscode\", model_provider=\"openai\"."
  temp_home_warning: "app-server warned it refuses to create helper binaries under a temporary dir; the implementation keeps the isolated home under the config dir instead."
evidence_files: "scratchpad desktop-probe1/{app.out.log,app2.out.log,srv.err.log}; window captures via PrintWindow(PW_RENDERFULLCONTENT) - screen-copy captures were discarded because the window could not be brought to the foreground and the copies showed the user's other windows."
cleanup: "Probe processes stopped (0 left), user instance 83404 untouched, the copied auth.json deleted."
